cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use Q-MAWS, please cite it using the metadata from this file."
type: software
title: "Q-MAWS: Quartet-based phylogeny from Minimal Absent Word Sets"
version: 0.0.0
authors:
  - given-names: Sudipta Kumar
    family-names: Das
    affiliation: "Department of Computer Science, AIUB"
    email: sudiptakumar400@gmail.com
    orcid: "https://orcid.org/0009-0000-7521-7763"
repository-code: "https://github.com/the-sudipta/q-maws"
abstract: >-
  Q-MAWS estimates a species tree from whole genomes without sequence
  alignment. It counts binary column patterns for every four-taxon subset
  of a minimal absent word character matrix, weights the three quartet
  topologies with a conditioned two-state likelihood, and combines the
  weighted quartets into one tree with a re-implementation of the wQFM
  algorithm.
keywords:
  - phylogenetics
  - alignment-free
  - minimal absent words
  - quartet amalgamation
